        "original_id": "21488361-a2ec-5ec2-a9c7-12cba3b2230e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Amy Lee, Jimi Hendrix, Dave Eggar, Dave Fortman\n- Organizations: Evanescence\n- Works: War Story, Indigo Grey, Voice from the Stone, \"Speak to Me\", \"Good Enough\"\n- Concepts: film scores, dive bomb, electric guitar influence\n\nFacts:\n- Amy Lynn Hartzler, née Lee, was born on December 13, 1981, and is professionally known as Amy Lee.\n- Amy Lee is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- Jimi Hendrix's mainstream career lasted only four years, but he is widely regarded as one of the most influential electric guitarists in popular music and one of the most celebrated musicians of the 20th century.\n- Jimi Hendrix is recognized as one of the pioneers of the dive bomb guitar technique.\n- During Evanescence's hiatus in 2013, Amy Lee began a film score career by composing the soundtrack for War Story, released in 2014, with cellist Dave Eggar.\n- Amy Lee and Dave Eggar also composed the soundtrack for Indigo Grey, released in 2015.\n- Amy Lee wrote the song \"Speak to Me\" for the film Voice from the Stone.\n- The Evanescence song \"Good Enough\" was written by Amy Lee and produced by Dave Fortman.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
